\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{Unit weights on the symmetric torus}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{On the periodic cubical torus, with both directions of every
axis and with every weight equal to #{1}, the form of
\ref{fdip-00PB} is the dot form on a free fibre of rank #{2d}.
Its reduction to rank #{d} is not taken here.}

\proof{
\p{Each axis contributes one forward edge and one backward edge
at every vertex, so the fibre is free of rank #{2d}. Every
weight is #{1}, which is a unit. \ref{fdip-00PC} says that the
form is nondegenerate of that rank, and \ref{fdip-00PB} says
that it is the sum of the squares of the edge coefficients.}
}
